# Copy to .env and fill in. Used by docker compose and by `bun run dev`.
#
# The file is the union of five independently deployable units — postgres,
# migrations, coordinator, web+caddy, provider. A single-host `docker compose
# up` wants all of it; a split deployment takes only its own section plus
# everything listed under "Shared across deploy units" below.

# ── Shared across deploy units ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# These values appear in more than one unit and must agree. What breaks:
#
#   POSTGRES_USER/PASSWORD/DB  postgres + coordinator + migrations, the latter
#                              two via DATABASE_URL. A mismatch is a login
#                              failure at boot.
#   DATABASE_URL               coordinator + migrations. Point them at
#                              different databases and the coordinator runs
#                              against an unmigrated schema.
#   PUBLIC_URL (host)          coordinator, caddy (SITE_ADDRESS), and the
#                              provider's coordinator_url in provider.yaml.
#                              Also the OAuth redirect host.
#   WEB_ORIGIN                 must be the origin the browser loads the SPA
#                              from — caddy's site, or :5173 in dev. Anything
#                              else fails CORS on every credentialed call.
#   FARM_PROVIDER_TOKEN        issued by the coordinator (/admin/providers),
#                              held by the provider. Never a coordinator var.

# ── images (every unit but postgres) ────────────────────────────────────────
# The compose files pull coordinator, web and provider from
# ghcr.io/dinip/device-farm/*, published when a release is created. Tags are the
# release version, the commit sha, `latest` (non-prereleases only), and `pr-N`
# for a PR labelled `build`. Prefer a version in production — `latest` moves
# under you on the next `docker compose pull`.
IMAGE_TAG=latest

# ── postgres ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_USER=farm                # also: coordinator, migrations (DATABASE_URL)
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=farm            # also: coordinator, migrations (DATABASE_URL)
POSTGRES_DB=farm                  # also: coordinator, migrations (DATABASE_URL)
# Published port on the host. postgres only — the compose network uses 5432.
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# ── migrations (packages/db) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE_URL=postgres://farm:farm@localhost:5432/farm   # also: coordinator
# Where the generated SQL lives. Only set when running migrations from
# somewhere other than the package — a container that ships them elsewhere.
# MIGRATIONS_DIR=

# ── coordinator ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reads DATABASE_URL above as well.
PORT=3000
# NODE_ENV=production
# Public origin of the coordinator. Must match the OAuth redirect URI host.
PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3000  # also: caddy (SITE_ADDRESS), provider.yaml
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API with credentials.
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173  # also: caddy (the site it serves the SPA on)
# openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=replace-me-with-at-least-32-characters-of-entropy

# Product name — the one place to change when the project is renamed. The SPA
# reads it over the API, so it belongs to the coordinator only; setting it on
# the web unit does nothing.
APP_NAME=Device Farm

# ── coordinator: sign-in ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Entra ID app registration. Redirect URI: <PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/callback/microsoft
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=common
# Bootstraps the first admin locally. Turn off once Microsoft sign-in works.
ENABLE_EMAIL_PASSWORD=true

# ── coordinator: session tokens (browser ↔ provider) ────────────────────────
# Ed25519 PKCS#8 PEM. Generated in memory at boot if unset, which invalidates
# live sessions on restart — set it in production. The provider never holds
# this; it verifies against the coordinator's published JWKS.
#   openssl genpkey -algorithm ed25519 -out session.pem
SESSION_TOKEN_PRIVATE_KEY=
SESSION_TOKEN_TTL=60
RESERVATION_TTL=900

# ── web + caddy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SPA bundle is static and takes no runtime configuration; everything below
# belongs to the proxy in front of it.
#
# ":80" for local, or a hostname like "farm.example.com" for automatic HTTPS.
# Must be the host in PUBLIC_URL / WEB_ORIGIN.
SITE_ADDRESS=:80
HTTP_PORT=80
HTTPS_PORT=443
# Dev only: where `bun run dev` proxies /api. Production has caddy do it.
# COORDINATOR_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── provider (docker compose --profile provider) ────────────────────────────
# A provider deployed on its own runs from docker-compose.provider.yml — the
# provider plus its own TLS terminator, nothing else. That shape needs two
# things this section does not cover: packages/provider/provider.yaml, carrying
# coordinator_url (the coordinator's PUBLIC_URL) and public_base_url (what the
# *browser* uses to reach this provider directly); and PROVIDER_SITE_ADDRESS,
# the same hostname as public_base_url, for its Caddy. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# PROVIDER_SITE_ADDRESS=lab-1.example.com
#
# That host needs no clone — those two files can live anywhere:
# PROVIDER_CONFIG=/etc/farm/provider.yaml
# PROVIDER_CADDYFILE=/etc/farm/Caddyfile
#
# Metrics carry no auth, so the standalone file publishes 9100 on loopback.
# Widen it only to an interface your monitoring reaches.
# METRICS_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# METRICS_PORT=9100
#
# Issue under /admin/providers in the UI. Shown once.
FARM_PROVIDER_TOKEN=
FARM_LOG=info
# Published port for the session plane — browsers connect here, not the
# coordinator. Must match the port in provider.yaml's bind/public_base_url.
# PROVIDER_PORT=7100

# macOS development only: Docker cannot pass USB through, so the iOS backend
# reaches the host's usbmuxd over the bridge in packages/provider/scripts.
# USBMUXD_BRIDGE_PORT=27015
